摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Use your logged-in web AI (DeepSeek, GLM, Kimi, Qwen, Doubao...) as model providers in DeepSeek Harness. Web models emit tool calls, DSH runs them under its native permission system, and results return to the same web session. No API keys.","id":"gh:1367182696","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-web-bridge","slug":"RSLN-creator/dsh-web-bridge","topics":["browser-automation","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","llm-adapter","playwright","webcode"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Use your logged-in web AI (DeepSeek, GLM, Kimi, Qwen, Doubao...) as model providers in DeepSeek Harn"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ess. Web models emit tool calls, DSH runs them under its native permission system, and results retur"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"n to the same web session. No API keys."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Harness Web Bridge"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** · 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Use your logged-in web AI — DeepSeek, GLM (Z.ai), Kimi, Qwen, Doubao — as model providers inside\nDee"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"pSeek Harness. Web models emit tool calls, DSH\nexecutes them under its native permission and approva"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"l system, and the results go back into the same\nweb session."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**No API keys.** It drives the site through your own browser login."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Status & risks (read this first)"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**Status**: this is a **work-in-progress project** — behavior and interfaces can change, and a site\n"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"redesign can break any site's channel at any time (keeping selectors and protocol teaching aligned\nw"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ith live pages is the daily work here). **Forks and PRs are welcome** — see\nCONTRIBUTING.md for the "},{"id":"p8s4","text":"commit-message shape and the local gates."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**Risks — evaluate for yourself before using**:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Risk | What it means |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| **Site ToS / account restriction** | The plugin drives your **logged-in web sessions** with automa"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"tion, which may violate a site's terms of service; accounts can be rate-limited or restricted — **on"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"e of the author's own DeepSeek web accounts has been restricted**. Pace your usage (the plugin ships"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" send gaps and backoff, but guarantees nothing). |\n| **Tool mode = prompt injection** | With \"local "},{"id":"p11s5","text":"tool calling\" enabled, the bridge injects tool-protocol teaching into the web conversation; that con"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"tent is **visible to the site**, and compared with plain browser use it widens the surface for being"},{"id":"p11s7","text":" flagged as automation. |\n| **Page redesigns break things** | Every site is \"the web page as a backe"},{"id":"p11s8","text":"nd\"; when a site ships a redesign its channel can break. |\n| **Data locality** | Login state lives o"},{"id":"p11s9","text":"nly in the plugin's **local** browser profile; no API keys, no telemetry, no cloud component. |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**Default mode (important)**: tool calling is **off by default** — the bridge is then a pure web\nses"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"sion: the web model receives exactly your words, identical to the browser (no prompt injection,\nno c"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"all replay). To let the web model call local tools, enable **Settings → Web Bridge → Local tool\ncall"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ing** (the first card) or the \"local tools\" pill under the composer — enabling asks for a\nconfirmati"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"on first. Tool calls, once produced, always execute under DSH's native permission system."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Why"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Most \"web model\" integrations are fragile in the same three ways: they scrape HTML, they lose the\nco"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"nversation when the page reloads, and they bypass the host's tool permissions. This plugin is\nbuilt "},{"id":"p14s3","text":"the other way around:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| Concern | How it is handled |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| **Tool permissions** | The web model only *proposes* calls. DSH runs them with its own permission "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"and approval system — the bridge cannot bypass it. |\n| **Session continuity** | A per-session cursor"},{"id":"p16s3","text":" keeps the web conversation alive across turns, across restarts, and after history rewrites. When th"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"e web session is lost the bridge replays the full first turn instead of silently starting over. |\n| "},{"id":"p16s5","text":"**Long prompts** | Over-threshold bodies are delivered as a file attachment, bypassing the composer'"},{"id":"p16s6","text":"s write-stall and truncation limits, with an automatic fallback to plain text if any step fails. |\n|"},{"id":"p16s7","text":" **Rate limits** | A configurable send gap (global **and per site**) plus automatic backoff-and-retr"},{"id":"p16s8","text":"y on the site's own rate-limit response. |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"- **Tool calling is an explicit switch (off by default).** By default the bridge is a pure web\nsessi"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"on (zero injection, zero replay). When enabled, each site is taught the tool-call shape it\nactually "},{"id":"p18s3","text":"accepts (DeepSeek's native token format, GLM's\n[代码示例省略，未执行]\npowershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add "},{"id":"p18s4","text":"s native token format, GLM's\n[代码示例省略，未执行]\npowershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-webcode-bridge"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]\npowershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add C:\\path\\to\\dsh-webcode-bridge-<version>.tgz"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]\npowershell\ncd package/dsh-webcode-bridge\npnpm install            # do NOT add --frozen-"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"lockfile, see doc/ci-cd.md\npnpm pack              # produces dsh-webcode-bridge-<version>.tgz"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"dsh: warning: dsh-webcode-bridge declares no dsh.bundle — installed as a plain dependency, not a pro"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ng: dsh-webcode-bridge declares no dsh.bundle — installed as a plain dependency, not a profile layer"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]\npowershell"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"# by package name\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-webcode-bridge"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"# or by the package subdirectory / a built tarball\ndsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/R"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"SLN-creator/dsh-web-bridge/tree/main/package/dsh-webcode-bridge\ndsh plugin --profile web add C:\\path"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"\\to\\dsh-webcode-bridge-<version>.tgz"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]\npowershell\ncd package/dsh-webcode-bridge\nnode test-mock/site-verify.mjs --list         "},{"id":"p26s2","text":" # every registered site\nnode test-mock/site-verify.mjs --site kimi     # one site\nnode test-mock/si"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"te-verify.mjs --site kimi --site qwen"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]\njson code-block shape, with fallback parsing from the thinking stream.\n- **Deep-link na"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"vigation is stopped by an Aliyun slider captcha**, so probes go through the driver path.\n- Two failu"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"re modes have been fixed: a stream that died mid-thinking produced an empty reply, and\ncall-fence ta"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"ils leaked into the reply body as garbage."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Read it as: **DeepSeek is the one to run all day; GLM is a good second opinion.** When GLM fails,\nre"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"try — attributable failures surface as coded messages rather than silent degradation."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"A few design notes worth knowing before you read the source."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"### Right sidebar, one origin per site"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Each site is served from `http://<siteId>.localhost:8931/`, so the pathname the site sees matches it"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"s\nreal site and SPA routers and root-relative assets work unchanged. The exception is **DeepSeek, wh"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"ich\nis always mounted at the relay root** — it validates the hostname, and a subdomain gives a blank"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"\n`Unknown hostname` page. `*.localhost` resolves to loopback, so the exposure surface is unchanged."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"Sites often load scripts and styles from a *different* origin with `crossorigin`, and that origin's\n"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"ten load scripts and styles from a *different* origin with `crossorigin`, and that origin's\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
